<% const a = report.analytics; const fmt = n => n === null || n === undefined ? '—' : n; %>
<section class="report-panel"><div class="report-panel-head"><div><div class="report-kicker">Common research definitions</div><h2>Participation & consumption</h2><p><%= a.compliance.note || 'Configure the study participation schedule to calculate compliance.' %></p></div></div>
<dl class="report-stats"><% [['Compliance',a.compliance.rate===null?'—':a.compliance.rate+'%'],['Completed / expected periods',a.compliance.expected===null?'—':a.compliance.completed+' / '+a.compliance.expected],['Occasions / participant week',fmt(a.avg_occasions_per_week)],['Average brand repertoire',a.repertoire==null?'—':a.repertoire.toFixed(2)]].forEach(([label,value])=>{ %><div class="report-stat"><dt><%= label %></dt><dd><%= value %></dd></div><% }) %></dl>
<p class="report-muted">Base: <%= fmt(a.base.respondents) %> eligible enrolled respondents; <%= fmt(a.base.valid_occasions) %> valid occasions. Repertoire is among brand consumers. Repeat means two or more observed occasions for that brand within this selection.</p>
<div style="overflow-x:auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable research results"><table class="report-table"><thead><tr><th>Brand</th><th>Consumers</th><th>Consumer incidence</th><th>Occasions</th><th>Occasion share</th><th>Repeat rate</th><th>Volume share</th></tr></thead><tbody><% a.brands.forEach(b=>{ %><tr><td><%= b.brand %></td><td><%= b.consumers %></td><td><%= fmt(b.consumer_incidence_pct) %>%</td><td><%= b.occasions %></td><td><%= fmt(b.share_of_occasions_pct) %>%</td><td><%= fmt(b.repeat_rate_pct) %>%</td><td><%= b.share_of_volume_pct===null?'Not configured / no valid volume':b.share_of_volume_pct+'%' %></td></tr><% }) %><% if(!a.brands.length){ %><tr><td colspan="7">No brand results available for this selection.</td></tr><% } %></tbody></table></div><p class="report-muted">Incidence uses enrolled respondents; occasion share uses valid occasions. Multiple brands can make occasion shares total over 100%. Volume share uses only single-brand occasions with a valid quantity in the configured comparable unit (<%= a.volume_unit||'not configured' %>).</p></section>
